  "id": "Compound::DB00571 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Propranolol exerts its pharmacological effects by binding to Cyp3a7, a cytochrome P450 enzyme that plays a critical role in drug metabolism. The evidence suggests that Cyp3a7 participates in multiple metabolic activities, including aromatase activity, oxidoreductase activity, and oxygen binding, all of which are mediated by Cyp3a4. This indicates that Cyp3a7 is functionally linked to Cyp3a4 through shared enzymatic roles, even though they are distinct proteins. The overlapping participation in these metabolic processes implies a potential functional interaction between the two, possibly through shared regulatory mechanisms or co-expression in certain tissues. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Cyp3a7 in the metabolic pathway of Propranolol, suggesting that Cyp3a4 may be a downstream target or a co-factor in the metabolic activation of the drug.",
